Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).

{
 "research_concepts": ["teammate DRIVE preceding PNR", "PNR possession points (PPP)", "play-type labeling from play-by-play", "derived play-type possession records", "sequence-based play-type context effects"],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "Does a teammate DRIVE preceding a PNR raise PNR PPP relative to matched PNRs without that preceding DRIVE?",
  "Are play-type labels derived from the stats API play-by-play and the graph database reliable enough to define DRIVE and PNR possessions?",
  "Do foul-ending and outcome-derived labels inflate PPP and bias the DRIVE-to-PNR contrast?",
  "What sample sizes per sequence cell are needed, and are they available?"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-025",
   "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
   "finding": "Play-type labeling audit found OTHER possessions with 36% foul endings and inflated PPP (FOUL_BUCKET); DRIVE was 12pp below the foul benchmark (FOUL_LEAK); PNR showed a 22% foul rate; only 335 of 50,668 possessions (0.7%) mapped to a real play type via initiation_type. Verdict recorded as artifact_found. Validation status: no_validation_recorded."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF40",
   "status_as_recorded": "not a hypothesis test",
   "finding": "Sequential premium scan. Same-player and teammate X->Y sequences were ranked by PPP premium over Y's baseline. Recorded cells include L. Doncic DRIVE->PNR +0.309 (n=53) and D. Bane DRIVE->PNR -0.324 (n=70). Mechanism recorded as unclear; limited by label/classification error and small sample."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-058",
   "status_as_recorded": "rejected",
   "finding": "Season-stability test of top sequential suppressors across 30 stars x 4 seasons (min n=20 per cell). Only 2/30 (7%) met the 75% same-top-suppressor stability rule. Negative teammate cells included Giannis->Lillard DRIVE->PNR -0.263 (n=31). Mechanism recorded as B_powered_null. Validation status: no_validation_recorded."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-058",
   "status_as_recorded": "untestable",
   "finding": "Observed on-ball defensive scheme labelling (ORL-DET G1). Confident label rates were 14.9% (DET, 10 of 67) and 3.3% (ORL, 2 of 60). switches_on was not populated by the matchups feed. Verdict failed_gate. Not a direct test of DRIVE-to-PNR, but evidences label-coverage limits in this data."
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-025",
   "what_failed": "Mapping possessions to play types via initiation_type and using PPP by play type as the basis for play-type efficiency claims.",
   "why": "Recorded as artifact: only 0.7% of possessions mapped to a real play type, and foul endings inflated OTHER PPP and shifted DRIVE and PNR PPP. The PPP differences reflected labelling and foul artifacts."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF40",
   "what_failed": "Ranking same-player and teammate X->Y sequence cells by PPP premium to find strong sequential effects.",
   "why": "Recorded as not a hypothesis test, with mechanism unclear and limits for label/classification error and small sample. Cell signs flip (e.g., DRIVE->PNR both positive and negative), so the scan does not yield a consistent effect."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-058",
   "what_failed": "Testing whether sequential suppressor premiums are stable across seasons.",
   "why": "Recorded as rejected by an adequately powered null: only 2/30 stars met the stability rule, and negative teammate cells were small (n about 31)."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-058",
   "what_failed": "Labelling on-ball defensive coverage from matchup and play-by-play fields.",
   "why": "Recorded as untestable (failed_gate): label rates were 3.3% to 14.9% and switches_on was unpopulated."
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "The derived play-type labels from initiation_type covered only about 0.7% of possessions in the audited set, so play-type labels as currently derived are not reliable for the question (FAM:SF-CHT-025).",
  "Foul endings are common in PNR and DRIVE-adjacent possessions and can bias PPP-based comparisons (FAM:SF-CHT-025).",
  "Prior sequence-premium scans found no stable teammate DRIVE->PNR effect; cell estimates were small-sample and sign-unstable (FAM:SF40, FAM:SF-APPA-058).",
  "Label coverage limits recur across play-type and defensive-scheme work in this data (FAM:SF-APPS-058)."
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "Whether a pooled teammate DRIVE-before-PNR contrast is positive. No returned record tests the pooled estimand with a validated label set and foul control.",
  "Whether the current graph-database labels are the same as those audited in FAM:SF-CHT-025; the record does not say whether it used the current build.",
  "The size of any true effect or the power of a pooled test. No record reports a pooled estimate with a confidence interval.",
  "Results for the 2025-26 playoffs, which were partial at the question date (2026-06-14)."
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "The question as posed (any teammate DRIVE preceding PNR raises PNR PPP) is a pooled claim about sequences, and its validity depends first on label validity.",
  "Foul-ending and possession-attribution artifacts (FAM:SF-CHT-025) would bias a naive DRIVE->PNR PPP contrast upward or downward, so a naive comparison cannot be interpreted.",
  "Sequence-cell scans (FAM:SF40, FAM:SF-APPA-058) imply a high multiple-comparisons risk if the question is answered by picking the best cell."
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "The records are truncated (cut in the retrieved text) and I did not read the full family records; full read_family text may change details.",
  "The audit in FAM:SF-CHT-025 may predate the current graph build. Current label coverage is unknown.",
  "The number of teammate DRIVE->PNR sequences in the 2022-23 to 2025-26 data is not reported.",
  "Whether a teammate DRIVE before a PNR means the same team, the same possession, or the immediately preceding possession is not defined in the question."
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes",
  "explanation": "Before retrieval, the plan was a standard sequence test with the derived labels. The retrieved records show that the derived play-type labels were recorded as an artifact source (0.7% coverage, foul-ending bias), that sequence scans of this kind were underpowered or unstable, and that a powered null occurred for stability. I therefore moved from proceed to do_not_proceed until the labels pass a validation gate. The question itself is not ruled out."
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": 0.3,
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {"code": "LABEL_ERROR", "text": "initiation_type mapped only 0.7% of possessions to a real play type in the audited set (FAM:SF-CHT-025); the DRIVE and PNR labels are not validated."},
   {"code": "OUTCOME_DERIVED_LABEL", "text": "Labels derived from play-by-play may be defined using outcomes such as points or fouls, which makes the PPP outcome circular if the label is not independent of the result."},
   {"code": "CONFOUNDING", "text": "Shot quality, shooter and defender quality, lineup, and foul endings all confound a DRIVE->PNR PPP contrast."},
   {"code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER", "text": "Per-cell sequence samples are about 30 to 70 (FAM:SF40, FAM:SF-APPA-058), which is too small for a reliable pooled or cell-level test without a pre-specified pooled estimand."}
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "partly",
  "cited": ["FAM:SF-CHT-025", "FAM:SF40", "FAM:SF-APPA-058", "FAM:SF-APPS-058"],
  "summary": "No returned record tests the pooled teammate DRIVE-before-PNR PPP claim with validated labels. FAM:SF40 and FAM:SF-APPA-058 touch on DRIVE->PNR cells with small, sign-unstable estimates and no pooled test. FAM:SF-CHT-025 shows the labels used to define the play types are unreliable. Prior work partly addresses related issues but does not answer the question as posed."
 },
 "risks": [
  {"code": "LABEL_ERROR", "text": "The teammate DRIVE and PNR labels may be mis-assigned, given 0.7% initiation_type coverage (FAM:SF-CHT-025)."},
  {"code": "OUTCOME_DERIVED_LABEL", "text": "Labels defined using points or foul outcomes would make the PPP contrast partly circular."},
  {"code": "CONFOUNDING", "text": "Shot quality, player quality, lineup, and foul endings confound the sequence effect."},
  {"code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER", "text": "Sequence-cell sample sizes near n=30 to 70 give wide intervals (FAM:SF40, FAM:SF-APPA-058)."},
  {"code": "MULTIPLE_TESTING", "text": "Scanning many player and teammate sequence cells and reporting the best ones inflates false positives (FAM:SF40)."},
  {"code": "PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE", "text": "Without a placebo sequence check, any PPP difference may reflect possession-type or foul-ending structure rather than a drive effect."},
  {"code": "DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY", "text": "Four seasons plus playoffs mix rule and style changes; season-to-season instability was recorded (FAM:SF-APPA-058)."},
  {"code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY", "text": "Defensive-matchup and scheme labels are sparse and partly unpopulated (FAM:SF-APPS-058), so matchup controls are unreliable."},
  {"code": "IMPLEMENTATION_BUG", "text": "Cross-source joins between the graph database and per-game files may misalign possessions; no reconciliation is recorded."}
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": 0.05,
  "rejected": 0.15,
  "untestable": 0.2,
  "artifact": 0.35,
  "uncertain": 0.25
 },
 "decision": "do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "Gate first: the label-validity estimand is the agreement rate between derived DRIVE and PNR labels and a manually audited sample. Only if that passes, the primary estimand is the within-team difference in PNR PPP (teammate-initiated PNR possessions) preceded by a teammate DRIVE possession versus preceded by a non-DRIVE possession, adjusted for controls.",
  "unit": "Possession (PNR possession), with the preceding possession as the sequence context; team-game as a clustering level.",
  "sample": "Regular seasons 2022-23 to 2024-25 and 2025-26 regular season (complete from 2026-04-13). Exclude 2025-26 playoffs, which were partial at 2026-06-14. Exclude fouled and non-shot-ending possessions as a sensitivity analysis.",
  "power": "Pre-specify minimum detectable effect before analysis from the pooled possession count after label validation. Not computed here; no pooled count is available in the records.",
  "controls": "Shooter and defender quality (player fixed effects or prior-season PPP), lineup, shot distance and type, foul-ending indicator, clock and score state, and defensive matchup where populated. Use team-game and player fixed effects.",
  "falsification": "Placebo sequences: a teammate non-DRIVE action (e.g., SPOT_UP or POST_UP) before PNR, and a DRIVE after the PNR. Expect null on both. Also check that the effect is absent when labels are randomly permuted within team-game.",
  "multiplicity": "One pre-specified pooled contrast as primary. All cell-level sequence results are exploratory and reported with false-discovery-rate control.",
  "decision_rule": "Proceed to the substantive test only if label validation agreement passes a pre-set threshold and the placebo checks are null. Call the effect supported only if the pooled primary contrast is positive with a 95% CI excluding zero and the placebo checks hold. Otherwise report rejected (if powered), artifact (if placebo or foul sensitivity removes the effect), or uncertain.",
  "data_version": "Data available as of 2026-06-14: 2022-23 to 2024-25 regular seasons and playoffs, 2025-26 regular season (complete), and 2025-26 playoffs excluded (partial at that date). Record the graph-database build version and reconcile it against the audited build in FAM:SF-CHT-025."
 }
}

